<title>BELGIUM: Legras says no hurry to open new EU grain tenders.</title>
<headline>Legras says no hurry to open new EU grain tenders.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Commission director-general for agriculture Guy Legras said on Tuesday the European Union was in no rush to open 1997/98 July-June grain export tenders, but no decision had yet been taken.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not in a hurry,&quot; he told reporters during EU farm ministers talks on the annual farm price package.  </p>
<p>However, he added that a preparatory meeting for this week's cereals management committee had not yet been held and he had still to be advised by his staff.</p>
<p>But he said any eventual decision to open tenders would not be implemented until published in the EU official journal, which could take a couple of weeks.</p>
<p>Legras noted that EU crop prospects had improved substantially following recent rain, but things could change before harvest.</p>
<p>--Luxembourg newsroom +352 57262</p>
